tel 1.0

# Flame's configuration for Soundness, so that `flame` started anywhere in this repository opens
# a REPL with Soundness already on its classpath, and needs no arguments.
#
# A RELATIVE classpath entry resolves against the project root — the directory holding
# `.pyrocosm` — not the invocation directory, so this works from any subdirectory. (fume's own
# config resolves relative entries against the invocation directory instead; the two tools
# differ here.) The jar is the umbrella test assembly `make test` builds, `./mill test.assembly`:
# every enabled library and its suites together, which is the widest classpath here. Before it
# has been built the REPL simply starts without it.
#
# This is the REPL for interactive use. `make doccheck` drives a separate `flame serve` daemon of
# its own, on a port it chooses, against the released flame pinned in etc/tools — it deliberately
# evaluates the tutorials against the last RELEASE rather than this working tree.
classpath out/test/assembly.dest/out.jar

# The presence of this directory is what opts the project into persistent prompt history, kept
# in `.pyrocosm/flame/history` (gitignored). This raises the limit from the default of 100.
history 1000
